      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<p><strong>NOTE</strong>: For students who have Calculus test credit, please note that the MCB major does NOT accept test credit to waive math requirements. If you are able to place out of Math 51, you may substitute Math 51 with an equivalent course to Stats 2, Stats 20, or Stats W21 to count towards the MCB major</p><p><br></p><p><strong>AP/IB information for the major in Molecular and Cell Biology for transfer students:</strong></p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">-Score of 4 or 5 on AP Chemistry satisfies CHEMISTRY 1A/1AL</p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">-Score of 4 or 5 on AP Biology satisfies BIOLOGY 1A/1AL + BIOLOGY 1B</p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">-Score of 5, 6, or 7 on IB Chemistry satisfies Chemistry 1A/1AL</p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">-Score of 5, 6, or 7 on IB Biology satisfies Biology 1B only</p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\"><br></p><p>The Molecular and Cell Biology Undergraduate Office discourages the use of AP, IB, or A-Level credit to waive lower-division courses. Lack of such coursework at the college level could result in poor performance in upper-division MCB courses. In addition, many health-related graduate and professional programs will not accept AP/IB scores in lieu of coursework completed at a college or university.</p>",
        "groupId": "bde0972e-7ada-468d-9a15-019982ad7dfd",
        "position": 5,
        "area": "General"
      }
